    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# GAMs: Modelos Aditivos Generalizados\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta ahora hemos estudiado diferentes maneras de introducir no linealidad cuando tenemos una variable predictora.\n",
        "\n",
        "Entre ellas:\n",
        "\n",
        "- regresión polinomial;\n",
        "- splines;\n",
        "- smoothing splines;\n",
        "- regresión local.\n",
        "\n",
        "Los **Modelos Aditivos Generalizados**, o GAMs, permiten extender estas ideas al caso en el que tenemos varias variables predictoras.\n",
        "\n",
        "La idea fundamental es reemplazar los términos lineales de una regresión múltiple por funciones flexibles.\n",
        "\n",
        "En una regresión lineal múltiple tenemos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$Y_i\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\beta_1X_{i1}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\beta_2X_{i2}\n",
        "+\\cdots+\n",
        "\\beta_pX_{ip}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon_i.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "En un GAM escribimos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$Y_i\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(X_{i1})\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_2(X_{i2})\n",
        "+\\cdots+\n",
        "f_p(X_{ip})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon_i.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Cada función $f_j$ puede tener una forma diferente.\n",
        "\n",
        "::::: diapositivas\n",
        "::: diapositivas-title\n",
        "📝 **Diapositivas**\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: diapositivas-body\n",
        "[Ver diapositivas GAMs](https://github.com/CursosENESJuriquilla/TS_Aprendizaje_de_Maquina_2027-1/blob/main/Material/2.8_GAMs.pdf)\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preparación\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos nuevamente el conjunto de datos `Wage`."
      ],
      "id": "e8deae81"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from ISLP import load_data\n",
        "\n",
        "from pygam import LinearGAM, LogisticGAM, s, l, f"
      ],
      "id": "02186e49",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Cargamos los datos."
      ],
      "id": "645e5cab"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Wage = load_data(\"Wage\")"
      ],
      "id": "726715e2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Revisamos las primeras observaciones."
      ],
      "id": "1b0e51e3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Wage.head()"
      ],
      "id": "21f30b7b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Nos interesarán principalmente:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `age`: edad;\n",
        "- `year`: año;\n",
        "- `education`: nivel educativo;\n",
        "- `wage`: salario.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preparar las variables\n",
        "\n",
        "`pygam` espera que la matriz de predictores sea bidimensional.\n",
        "\n",
        "Además, para una variable categórica como `education`, necesitamos una representación numérica.\n",
        "\n",
        "Primero revisamos sus categorías."
      ],
      "id": "1369f002"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Wage[\"education\"].cat.categories"
      ],
      "id": "49bc7c27",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos obtener códigos enteros con:"
      ],
      "id": "7f04ea98"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "education_code = Wage[\"education\"].cat.codes"
      ],
      "id": "8202c207",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos la matriz de predictores."
      ],
      "id": "9df159bd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X = np.column_stack([\n",
        "    Wage[\"age\"],\n",
        "    Wage[\"year\"],\n",
        "    education_code\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "y = Wage[\"wage\"].to_numpy()"
      ],
      "id": "81871414",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Revisamos las dimensiones."
      ],
      "id": "4ced70a5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X.shape"
      ],
      "id": "c96d272c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La matriz tiene tres columnas:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$X_1=\\text{age},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "X_2=\\text{year},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "X_3=\\text{education}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## Nuestro primer GAM\n",
        "\n",
        "Consideremos el modelo\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{wage}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(\\text{age})\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_2(\\text{year})\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_3(\\text{education})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos:\n",
        "\n",
        "- un término suavizado para `age`;\n",
        "- un término suavizado para `year`;\n",
        "- un término categórico para `education`.\n",
        "\n",
        "En `pygam` podemos escribir:"
      ],
      "id": "a4e6934f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(0) +\n",
        "    s(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "02e06948",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Aquí:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `s(0)` aplica un suavizador a la primera columna;\n",
        "- `s(1)` aplica un suavizador a la segunda columna;\n",
        "- `f(2)` trata la tercera columna como una variable categórica.\n",
        "\n",
        "Ajustamos el modelo."
      ],
      "id": "160f77de"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam.fit(X, y)"
      ],
      "id": "87b9f673",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## ¿Qué significa cada término?\n",
        "\n",
        "Nuestro modelo tiene la forma\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat y\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\hat\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_1(\\text{age})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_2(\\text{year})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_3(\\text{education}).$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto significa que la predicción se construye sumando contribuciones separadas.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat y\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\text{intercepto}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{efecto de age}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{efecto de year}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{efecto de education}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "La palabra **aditivo** proviene precisamente de esta estructura.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Efecto parcial de `age`\n",
        "\n",
        "Una de las principales ventajas de los GAMs es que podemos examinar el efecto de cada predictor por separado.\n",
        "\n",
        "Construimos una malla para el término correspondiente a `age`."
      ],
      "id": "f0bdd36e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "XX = gam.generate_X_grid(\n",
        "    term=0\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "3d864886",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Calculamos el efecto parcial."
      ],
      "id": "f7aaeab1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "partial_age = gam.partial_dependence(\n",
        "    term=0,\n",
        "    X=XX\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "5eea7c50",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "También podemos obtener intervalos de confianza."
      ],
      "id": "69d8ec94"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pdep_age, confi_age = gam.partial_dependence(\n",
        "    term=0,\n",
        "    X=XX,\n",
        "    width=0.95\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "820e37b8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Visualizamos el efecto."
      ],
      "id": "373382f4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX[:, 0],\n",
        "    pdep_age,\n",
        "    linewidth=3\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX[:, 0],\n",
        "    confi_age[:, 0],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX[:, 0],\n",
        "    confi_age[:, 1],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Efecto parcial sobre wage\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Efecto parcial de age\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "01576fca",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### ¿Cómo interpretar esta gráfica?\n",
        "\n",
        "La curva representa la contribución estimada de `age` al salario.\n",
        "\n",
        "No representa directamente el salario esperado.\n",
        "\n",
        "Representa\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat f_1(\\text{age}),$$\n",
        "\n",
        "es decir, la contribución de la edad después de considerar simultáneamente los demás términos del modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: callout-note\n",
        "Un valor positivo de $\\hat f_1(\\text{age})$ indica que esa edad contribuye a aumentar la predicción respecto al nivel promedio del modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Un valor negativo indica una contribución en sentido contrario.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Efecto parcial de `year`\n",
        "\n",
        "Repetimos el procedimiento para `year`."
      ],
      "id": "917f4e1e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "XX_year = gam.generate_X_grid(\n",
        "    term=1\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "db217124",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pdep_year, confi_year = gam.partial_dependence(\n",
        "    term=1,\n",
        "    X=XX_year,\n",
        "    width=0.95\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "aeeec26b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX_year[:, 1],\n",
        "    pdep_year,\n",
        "    linewidth=3\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX_year[:, 1],\n",
        "    confi_year[:, 0],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX_year[:, 1],\n",
        "    confi_year[:, 1],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Año\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Efecto parcial sobre wage\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Efecto parcial de year\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "94f80bdf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿El efecto de `year` parece claramente no lineal?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip collapse=\"true\" icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## Discusión\n",
        "\n",
        "Es posible que el efecto de `year` tenga una forma bastante cercana a una recta.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto plantea una pregunta importante:\n",
        "\n",
        "> ¿Realmente necesitamos un término no lineal para `year`?\n",
        "\n",
        "Más adelante compararemos modelos para responderlo.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Efecto de una variable categórica\n",
        "\n",
        "El término\n",
        "\n",
        "``` python\n",
        "f(2)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "corresponde a `education`.\n",
        "\n",
        "A diferencia de `age` y `year`, `education` no es una variable continua. Por tanto, no queremos construir una curva sobre una malla de muchos valores.\n",
        "\n",
        "Queremos estimar una contribución para **cada nivel educativo**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Primero revisamos las categorías."
      ],
      "id": "eb06df0b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "education_levels = Wage[\"education\"].cat.categories\n",
        "\n",
        "education_levels"
      ],
      "id": "9926ff53",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Recordemos que `pygam` trabaja con los códigos numéricos de estas categorías:"
      ],
      "id": "c32a41d6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "education_codes = np.arange(len(education_levels))\n",
        "\n",
        "education_codes"
      ],
      "id": "38e4d0e0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora construiremos una matriz con una fila para cada nivel educativo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Mantendremos `age` y `year` en valores representativos y cambiaremos únicamente `education`."
      ],
      "id": "5c2cb160"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_education = np.column_stack([\n",
        "    np.repeat(Wage[\"age\"].mean(), len(education_levels)),\n",
        "    np.repeat(Wage[\"year\"].mean(), len(education_levels)),\n",
        "    education_codes\n",
        "])"
      ],
      "id": "08ffce80",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos revisar la matriz."
      ],
      "id": "6fd8c85d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_education"
      ],
      "id": "2953a2f4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Cada fila corresponde a un nivel educativo distinto, mientras que `age` y `year` permanecen constantes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Calculamos ahora el efecto parcial del término categórico."
      ],
      "id": "fd30f244"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pdep_education, confi_education = gam.partial_dependence(\n",
        "    term=2,\n",
        "    X=X_education,\n",
        "    width=0.95\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "b480732c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos revisar los resultados."
      ],
      "id": "e24eb8eb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pdep_education"
      ],
      "id": "912315e8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora tenemos exactamente un valor por cada nivel educativo."
      ],
      "id": "1ed30fea"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "len(education_levels), len(pdep_education)"
      ],
      "id": "abcb6ed2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Representamos las contribuciones."
      ],
      "id": "6ffc8407"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "x_pos = np.arange(len(education_levels))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.errorbar(\n",
        "    x_pos,\n",
        "    pdep_education,\n",
        "    yerr=[\n",
        "        pdep_education - confi_education[:, 0],\n",
        "        confi_education[:, 1] - pdep_education\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    fmt=\"o\",\n",
        "    capsize=4\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.axhline(\n",
        "    y=0,\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\",\n",
        "    alpha=0.5\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xticks(\n",
        "    x_pos,\n",
        "    education_levels,\n",
        "    rotation=45,\n",
        "    ha=\"right\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Nivel educativo\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Efecto parcial sobre wage\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Efecto parcial de education\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "69cc43b4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## ¿Cómo interpretar esta gráfica?\n",
        "\n",
        "Cada punto representa la contribución estimada de un nivel educativo al modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Es decir, estamos visualizando\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat f_3(\\text{education}).$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Un valor mayor indica una contribución más positiva a la predicción de `wage`, una vez considerados simultáneamente los efectos de `age` y `year`.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: callout-note\n",
        "El eje vertical representa el **efecto parcial**, no el salario predicho directamente.\n",
        "\n",
        "El salario estimado completo se obtiene sumando\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat y\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\hat\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_1(\\text{age})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_2(\\text{year})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_3(\\text{education}).$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Interpretar el modelo de manera conjunta\n",
        "\n",
        "Recordemos que el modelo es\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat y\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\hat\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_1(\\text{age})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_2(\\text{year})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\hat f_3(\\text{education}).$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Supongamos conceptualmente que para una persona obtenemos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat\\beta_0=100,$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat f_1(\\text{age})=15,$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat f_2(\\text{year})=5,$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat f_3(\\text{education})=20.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Entonces\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat y\n",
        "=\n",
        "100+15+5+20\n",
        "=\n",
        "140.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Cada término aporta una contribución separada.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Predicciones con el GAM\n",
        "\n",
        "Una vez ajustado el modelo podemos hacer predicciones."
      ],
      "id": "1346e54a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y_hat = gam.predict(X)"
      ],
      "id": "ed14dae8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos comparar valores observados y predichos."
      ],
      "id": "6dad595f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 7))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    y_hat,\n",
        "    alpha=0.4\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "min_val = min(y.min(), y_hat.min())\n",
        "max_val = max(y.max(), y_hat.max())\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    [min_val, max_val],\n",
        "    [min_val, max_val],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Wage observado\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Wage predicho\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Valores observados vs. predichos\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "83731393",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Si las predicciones fueran perfectas, todos los puntos caerían sobre la diagonal.\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Necesitamos que todos los términos sean no lineales?\n",
        "\n",
        "Un GAM no obliga a que todos los predictores sean suavizados.\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos combinar términos lineales y no lineales.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{wage}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(\\text{age})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\beta_2\\text{year}\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_3(\\text{education})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "En `pygam`:"
      ],
      "id": "ec616001"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_year_linear = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(0) +\n",
        "    l(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "3e4c848f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ajustamos el modelo."
      ],
      "id": "61e52101"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_year_linear.fit(X, y)"
      ],
      "id": "7bb86ed2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora `age` sigue teniendo una relación flexible, pero `year` entra linealmente.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tres modelos para estudiar `year`\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos comparar tres posibilidades.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Modelo 1: sin `year`\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{wage}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(\\text{age})\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_3(\\text{education})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon.$$"
      ],
      "id": "5b9bf57a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_no_year = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(0) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "gam_no_year.fit(X, y)"
      ],
      "id": "0d4ae436",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Modelo 2: `year` lineal\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{wage}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(\\text{age})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\beta_2\\text{year}\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_3(\\text{education})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon.$$"
      ],
      "id": "5013aff4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_year_linear = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(0) +\n",
        "    l(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "gam_year_linear.fit(X, y)"
      ],
      "id": "724c3dc9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Modelo 3: `year` suavizado\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{wage}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(\\text{age})\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_2(\\text{year})\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_3(\\text{education})\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon.$$"
      ],
      "id": "2d11ff02"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_year_smooth = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(0) +\n",
        "    s(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "gam_year_smooth.fit(X, y)"
      ],
      "id": "57cc9ae1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Comparación de modelos\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos comparar la calidad de ajuste utilizando criterios como AIC."
      ],
      "id": "97277687"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "comparison = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Modelo\": [\n",
        "        \"Sin year\",\n",
        "        \"Year lineal\",\n",
        "        \"Year suavizado\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"AIC\": [\n",
        "        gam_no_year.statistics_[\"AIC\"],\n",
        "        gam_year_linear.statistics_[\"AIC\"],\n",
        "        gam_year_smooth.statistics_[\"AIC\"]\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "comparison"
      ],
      "id": "89251121",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Recordemos que, en términos generales, un AIC más pequeño indica un mejor compromiso entre ajuste y complejidad.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Preguntas\n",
        "\n",
        "1.  ¿Mejora el modelo al incluir `year`?\n",
        "2.  ¿Vale la pena modelar `year` de manera no lineal?\n",
        "3.  ¿El aumento en flexibilidad produce una mejora importante?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip collapse=\"true\" icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## Solución\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Una observación sobre ANOVA en GAMs\n",
        "\n",
        "En el libro se comparan modelos mediante pruebas tipo ANOVA.\n",
        "\n",
        "La idea conceptual es muy importante:\n",
        "\n",
        "podemos comparar modelos anidados para evaluar si un predictor\n",
        "\n",
        "- debe excluirse;\n",
        "- debe aparecer linealmente;\n",
        "- necesita un efecto no lineal.\n",
        "\n",
        "Conceptualmente podemos comparar\n",
        "\n",
        "$$M_1:\n",
        "\\quad\n",
        "Y\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(X_1)\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_3(X_3)\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon,$$\n",
        "\n",
        "contra\n",
        "\n",
        "$$M_2:\n",
        "\\quad\n",
        "Y\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(X_1)\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\beta_2X_2\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_3(X_3)\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon,$$\n",
        "\n",
        "y posteriormente contra\n",
        "\n",
        "$$M_3:\n",
        "\\quad\n",
        "Y\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(X_1)\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_2(X_2)\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_3(X_3)\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\varepsilon.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "La primera pregunta:\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Aporta información $X_2$?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "La segunda pregunta:\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Necesitamos que el efecto de $X_2$ sea no lineal?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "Nosotros utilizaremos principalmente criterios de ajuste y visualización, pero la lógica de comparación de modelos es la misma.\n",
        "\n",
        "### ¿Qué ocurre con `age`?\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos hacer exactamente el mismo razonamiento para `age`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Consideremos:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$M_1:\n",
        "\\quad\n",
        "\\text{sin age},$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$M_2:\n",
        "\\quad\n",
        "\\text{age lineal},$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$M_3:\n",
        "\\quad\n",
        "\\text{age suavizado}.$$"
      ],
      "id": "de5ca247"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_no_age = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ").fit(X, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "gam_age_linear = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    l(0) +\n",
        "    s(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ").fit(X, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "gam_age_smooth = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(0) +\n",
        "    s(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ").fit(X, y)"
      ],
      "id": "2d941cba",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Comparamos."
      ],
      "id": "09c3d35b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "comparison_age = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Modelo\": [\n",
        "        \"Sin age\",\n",
        "        \"Age lineal\",\n",
        "        \"Age suavizado\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"AIC\": [\n",
        "        gam_no_age.statistics_[\"AIC\"],\n",
        "        gam_age_linear.statistics_[\"AIC\"],\n",
        "        gam_age_smooth.statistics_[\"AIC\"]\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "comparison_age"
      ],
      "id": "e1d89c11",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿La evidencia a favor de un efecto no lineal de `age` parece más fuerte que para `year`?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## GAMs para clasificación\n",
        "\n",
        "Los GAMs también pueden utilizarse cuando la respuesta es binaria.\n",
        "\n",
        "Construiremos una variable que indique si el salario es superior a 250."
      ],
      "id": "aac3e15d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "high_earn = (\n",
        "    Wage[\"wage\"] > 250\n",
        ").astype(int)"
      ],
      "id": "405b6973",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos revisar la frecuencia de ambas clases."
      ],
      "id": "b77f1797"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "high_earn.value_counts()"
      ],
      "id": "110c274b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Nuestro objetivo es modelar\n",
        "\n",
        "$$P(\n",
        "\\text{wage}>250\n",
        "\\mid\n",
        "\\text{age},\n",
        "\\text{year},\n",
        "\\text{education}\n",
        ").$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## GAM logístico\n",
        "\n",
        "En regresión logística tradicional tenemos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\log\n",
        "\\left(\n",
        "\\frac{p(X)}{1-p(X)}\n",
        "\\right)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\beta_1X_1\n",
        "+\\cdots+\n",
        "\\beta_pX_p.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "En un GAM logístico reemplazamos algunos términos lineales por funciones flexibles:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\log\n",
        "\\left(\n",
        "\\frac{p(X)}{1-p(X)}\n",
        "\\right)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_1(X_1)\n",
        "+\n",
        "f_2(X_2)\n",
        "+\\cdots+\n",
        "f_p(X_p).$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Ajustamos:"
      ],
      "id": "7a8d4865"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_logit = LogisticGAM(\n",
        "    s(0) +\n",
        "    s(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "5990ed60",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_logit.fit(\n",
        "    X,\n",
        "    high_earn\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "f62c8cad",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Un problema con categorías poco representadas\n",
        "\n",
        "Antes de interpretar el modelo, conviene revisar la relación entre `education` y la respuesta."
      ],
      "id": "19ce4d6d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pd.crosstab(\n",
        "    Wage[\"education\"],\n",
        "    high_earn\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "0506db34",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Puede ocurrir que alguna categoría no contenga observaciones de una de las clases.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, si en un determinado nivel educativo no existen individuos con\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{wage}>250,$$\n",
        "\n",
        "el modelo puede tener dificultades para estimar adecuadamente el efecto de esa categoría.\n",
        "\n",
        "Este fenómeno está relacionado con problemas de **separación** en modelos logísticos.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Ajuste restringido\n",
        "\n",
        "Para evitar ese problema podemos excluir una categoría sin observaciones positivas."
      ],
      "id": "7ef87110"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "mask = (\n",
        "    Wage[\"education\"] !=\n",
        "    Wage[\"education\"].cat.categories[0]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "Wage_sub = Wage.loc[mask].copy()"
      ],
      "id": "425c4d94",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Reconstruimos las variables."
      ],
      "id": "2d098201"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "education_sub = (\n",
        "    Wage_sub[\"education\"]\n",
        "    .cat.remove_unused_categories()\n",
        "    .cat.codes\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "X_sub = np.column_stack([\n",
        "    Wage_sub[\"age\"],\n",
        "    Wage_sub[\"year\"],\n",
        "    education_sub\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "high_earn_sub = (\n",
        "    Wage_sub[\"wage\"] > 250\n",
        ").astype(int)"
      ],
      "id": "9cee51dd",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ajustamos nuevamente."
      ],
      "id": "72ec47a4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_logit_sub = LogisticGAM(\n",
        "    s(0) +\n",
        "    s(1) +\n",
        "    f(2)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "gam_logit_sub.fit(\n",
        "    X_sub,\n",
        "    high_earn_sub\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "9ecc1256",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Efecto parcial de `age` en clasificación"
      ],
      "id": "27cafef4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "XX_age_logit = gam_logit_sub.generate_X_grid(\n",
        "    term=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "pdep_age_logit, confi_age_logit = gam_logit_sub.partial_dependence(\n",
        "    term=0,\n",
        "    X=XX_age_logit,\n",
        "    width=0.95\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "3e940ff0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX_age_logit[:, 0],\n",
        "    pdep_age_logit,\n",
        "    linewidth=3\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX_age_logit[:, 0],\n",
        "    confi_age_logit[:, 0],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    XX_age_logit[:, 0],\n",
        "    confi_age_logit[:, 1],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Efecto parcial\")\n",
        "plt.title(\n",
        "    \"Efecto parcial de age sobre la clasificación\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fe6926a3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Importante\n",
        "\n",
        "En un GAM logístico, el eje vertical no representa directamente una probabilidad.\n",
        "\n",
        "La función contribuye a\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\log\n",
        "\\left(\n",
        "\\frac{p}{1-p}\n",
        "\\right).$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por tanto, debemos interpretar principalmente la forma de la curva:\n",
        "\n",
        "- regiones donde la contribución aumenta;\n",
        "- regiones donde disminuye;\n",
        "- cambios no lineales;\n",
        "- regiones con mayor incertidumbre.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Probabilidades predichas\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos obtener probabilidades directamente con:"
      ],
      "id": "aa4566c3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "probabilities = gam_logit_sub.predict_proba(\n",
        "    X_sub\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "b7e3de1e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Revisamos algunas."
      ],
      "id": "6d3bec62"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "probabilities[:10]"
      ],
      "id": "c6791320",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Estas sí corresponden a valores entre 0 y 1.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Clasificación\n",
        "\n",
        "También podemos producir clases predichas."
      ],
      "id": "a34f2714"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "predicted_class = gam_logit_sub.predict(\n",
        "    X_sub\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "35144cea",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos construir una tabla de contingencia."
      ],
      "id": "47d1111d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pd.crosstab(\n",
        "    high_earn_sub,\n",
